{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions","id":32279,"title":"How to get around the racial restrictions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-18T04:05:13-08:00","id":32279,"title":"How to get around the racial restrictions","content":"While there are some advantages to having a more tightly geographically / historically focused origin for all your PCs, perhaps that just isn't working for your campaign, or your PC. But how to fix that, while staying in genre?<br /> <br /> At some point, somewhere, your character got killed REAL GOOD. <br /> <br /> Maybe they were devoured, or ground to dust, or banished by somebody who knew how. Regardless, their original, Iremite, body was utterly and completely lost. <br /> <br /> Which means that their cult had to find a new body - and that could be anybody,almost anywhen or where. Sure, the book says that the ST is recommended to levy some penalties for those kind of shenanigans, but they are optional (and, to me, intended as consequences for some PC getting themselves ground up in game). Perhaps after a rebirth cycle or two, those penalties don't trouble you anymore, because the souls have more fully fused?<br /> <br /> Let's say you got killed really good AND your cult disbanded. Still no problem. A little bit of Ren magic, either accomplished by some Mummy sent to solve the problem or your Judge directly or even as a side effect of some relic... and suddenly some mostly crazy (but somewhat charismatic) person out there gets the idea that through whispered dreams and old gods they can create a servant / protector by performing a ritual on a (conveniently) dead body. Or ancient spirits are showing them the way to return their love to life, by fusing her preserved form with another soul fragment. New body, new cult. You just can't kill a Mummy, not forever. There's /always/ a way back.<br /> <br /> Viola! You've got a totally legit backstory which gets you any body you want, with the potential for some misinformation about your true origins (corrected with rising Memory) if the ST is into that sort of thing. <br /> <br /> (In my campaign the assumption is a very solid percentage of Mummies have lost their original bodies at some point - it's not that hard to do. Enough so that there's tension between the purebloods and mixed-bloods.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T15:32:45-08:00","id":32765,"title":"","content":"There are some storyline stretches that allow for a bit more racial diversity when it comes to Irem. For example, in my groups, during the twilight of the Empire's heights it was making (foolish) campaigns to the North and East to help expand. While they didnt get too far, they did manage to capture a few &quot;barbaric Northmen&quot; and send them back to Irem. While most stayed slaves, one of the NPCs of my group was a warlord who evaded execution and slavery by joining a guild and converting to worship of irem's gods. Of course, this isnt a common event (in my groups, hes often referenced as THE white mummy), but its enough to justify maybe one true caucasian mummy, or a true hindi one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T15:52:54-08:00","id":32780,"title":"","content":"I don't think this idea works quite right, the sahu appears to be created from the memory of the Mummy, not the actual remains.<br /> <br /> I guess you could still make it work, but it's not seamless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T16:05:29-08:00","id":32788,"title":"","content":"Its legit if you want to play a Mummy of whatever ethnic features with the explanation that the Arisen have been around a long time and they may have been through one or more cases where they needed an outright new body. I would allow it. Starting Characters in my opinion are not even necessarily as strong as they ever been, they are as strong as they remember being, so doing games where you uncover and get bonus EXP with memories could work as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T21:01:19-08:00","id":32943,"title":"","content":"That's what the concept of the sahu is for. A mummy's sahu is defined influenced by her memories. If she's spend the last couple centuries in Cambodia, and if she has stronger memories of Cambodia than of the Nameless Empire, then she'll look Cambodian, no matter her actual origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T05:01:46-08:00","id":33076,"title":"","content":"I don't necessarily think the memory is that plastic. The mummy with the native Alaskan cult in the intro was still obviously Nubian. And even if it were that malleable, the mummy would return to form pretty quickly as soon as they regained any amount of memory. I guess the question is though, why does one want to get around the restriction? Like, why is it important that your mummy not be North African?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:11:26-08:00","id":33393,"title":"","content":"Yeah the corebook had it that the Sahu changes, but its slow and subtle, for the strong changes you need something more then amnesia and nostalgia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:39:38-08:00","id":33419,"title":"","content":"The section on getting an outright new body says that your original soul is fused to the body's memories / psyche. Such that 'things like cellphones and democracy are as natural to you now as slavery and sacrifice were to you before.' This would shape not just your memory of yourself (since you have an overlapping set of memories now), but the actual physical remains. <br /> <br /> The sahu might be shaped from your memory (once your power drops below 9 or 10 and you develop the protective visage), but it seems to be clearly the remains of your original body, which is why it's a big deal to lose that body. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions?p=33076#post33076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess the question is though, why does one want to get around the restriction? Like, why is it important that your mummy not be North African?</div> </div> </div> </div>As for why, why not? Why should it be necessary that every Chronicle and every character be focused on those themes? I was just offering options for people who wanted more options. Maybe somebody wants to play a character steeped more in the Incan tradition? Or somebody from the Victorian / Rosicrucian tradition who has false memories? It was a stated situation that some Mummies think they're actually Egyptian, why not Mongolian? <br /> <br /> Plus, as I mentioned earlier, assuming that a significant number of mummies have lost their original bodies over time and needed to pick up new local bodies creates the possibility of political dynamics between those groups - the originals and the successors. One more reason for Mummies to hate each other! To me, increasing the diversity of representation, character backstory possibilities and giving new dynamics to hang story hooks off of seems like a win. It might not be what every ST is looking at - I can definitely see some campaigns which focus more tightly on the whole standard Iremite culture discordance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:58:21-08:00","id":39949,"title":"","content":"&quot;Mummy&quot; is not a generic archetypal monster even if the same term is used in English for a variety of preserved bodies. Having Incan mummies is a thematically incoherent addition to the game for the sake of a linguistic quirk. Mummy: The Curse is not about how it's weird that English uses a word derived from a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses for all preserved corpses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:10:35-08:00","id":40196,"title":"","content":"Do we have any solid idea of how wide and expansive the empire was? I mean, the traditional mesopotamia, egypt, libya, and nubia are obvious, but.. how far east did they expand? Did they have distant outposts? Did they make an effort to build far off tombs for special mummies? Could the empire have potentially expanded as large as Persia's? Or Alexander the Great? In my mummy, the one white mummy is a very rare case of a slave that was able to rise in ranks. He may be the only one, or he couldve even become twice arisen and simply mistaken his memories. He certainly does get that assumption from most of the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-19T14:36:53-08:00","id":53464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions?p=40196#post40196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any solid idea of how wide and expansive the empire was? I mean, the traditional mesopotamia, egypt, libya, and nubia are obvious, but.. how far east did they expand? Did they have distant outposts? Did they make an effort to build far off tombs for special mummies? Could the empire have potentially expanded as large as Persia's? Or Alexander the Great? In my mummy, the one white mummy is a very rare case of a slave that was able to rise in ranks. He may be the only one, or he couldve even become twice arisen and simply mistaken his memories. He certainly does get that assumption from most of the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sidebar on Ethnicity in the Origin section says outright that the Nameless Empire expanded across most of North Africa, down towards Central Africa via what is now Sudan, into the Levant and across Asia Minor. If they mean the whole of Asia Minor, that's pretty damn big. And they don't precisely identify the limits of what they meant by 'Central Africa'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 01-19-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T00:40:07-08:00","id":55306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions?p=39949#post39949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mummy&quot; is not a generic archetypal monster even if the same term is used in English for a variety of preserved bodies. Having Incan mummies is a thematically incoherent addition to the game for the sake of a linguistic quirk. Mummy: The Curse is not about how it's weird that English uses a word derived from a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses for all preserved corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. HOWEVER - it easily can fit for any culture that engaged in human deification-sacrifice-mummification/continued-worship, to have an Arisen who's previous body got completely destroyed, and their cult sacrificed a chosen one to be mummified as a new incarnation of their god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:15:44-08:00","id":56408,"title":"","content":"I've found few of my players doubt the concept that the rare, occassional slave from across the black sea or the persian desert made its way into Irem, and that some were worthy of mummification. even then, however, they were almost wholly acculturated, and a VERY distinct minority (My indoeuropean mummy claims to have been the only Northern anyone he has ever met remembers and is always facing shock and confusion over it). Of course, this is because my Irem was running exploration/exploitation expeditions across the Black and Mediterranean seas, as well as the Caucasus mountains. There, they met from strong reistance from the indo-europeans, who at the time were beginning the expansions across europe. The &quot;sea people&quot; and the &quot;horse people&quot; were disorganized, but driven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T16:38:41-08:00","id":56419,"title":"","content":"I like the cut of your jib, Cleverest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:13:58-08:00","id":56689,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I may not be very conservative in my estimate's of Irem's power. I tend to be extreme, thinking they had outposts and border colonies as far away as modern Afghsnistan, to trade with the Indus River People. Similarly, even at the height of their Empire, they faced the &quot;north and south problem&quot;. North of the black sea were the &quot;kurgan&quot; people, the Northmen who claim Irem stole the technology of horses and chariots from them (their skill certainly supports this). These northmen often crossed the black and mediterranean seas to raid border colonies of Irem, introduing their &quot;proto indoeuropean language&quot; and culture. Similarly, the Empire could not conquer the Nile all the way to its source. While the Lands of Kush were a part of the Empire, the tribes at the Nile's source were impregnable. While the legends of the birthplace of humanity, in a lush &quot;garden&quot; (in the Congo, likely) may have been a goal of the Iremites, they never fully broke through the north or south, unlike the east and west.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:48:06-08:00","id":56712,"title":"","content":"Well, it would certainly explain why their expansion stopped at the places it did besides limits of maintaining communication across those distances even with magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:58:33-08:00","id":56718,"title":"","content":"Right. Afghanistan and Pakistan are notoriously difficult to conquer, and the book suggests that the Yellow, Indus, and Yangtzee river people TRADED with Irem, but were not in their empire. Similarly, the notion that &quot;fair skinned folk&quot; were outside of their control as well, despite their relative proximity compared to the Upper Nile and deep Kush, means that they were... difficult to contain. Like the nomads of mesopotamia, but without the Kir-en-Gar city-states as core targets. History suggests that the proto-indo-europeans were the first to tame horses, first viking/pirates, first wandering gypsy style culture (probably evolved from preneolithic lifestyle).. they went from a small culture on the north side of the black sea, to a linguistic group that went epidemic across europe and beyond that even Irem could not stop. Similarly, I can imagine a lot of tasty Heart of Darkness style stories, as Iremites sail up the Nile through conquered Nubian territories, into the unconquered lands held by tribes older than the Empire, trying to find the source of the Nile, and the source of Humanity itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T01:11:00-08:00","id":67779,"title":"","content":"I tend to try to avoid playing Minorities. Why? I'm on a lot of chat sites, and the last thing I want to do is offend someone by being overly stereotypical, or getting things wrong with cultural aspects and whatnot. I'll note before saying this; I am hyperbolizing to get my point across, but how do you think an African American fellow would react to a nerdy white guy playing a Black PC with a love for fried chicken? <br /> <br /> It wouldn't go over so well, now I'm not THAT stupid, but the same general theme of issues is something I try to avoid. And I doubt I'm the only one concerned about not offending people and causing problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:15:32-08:00","id":68036,"title":"","content":"Whilst I can see what you're getting at, Mummies aren't similar to any existing ethnic minority that I'm aware of. Any stereotypes about them are going to be those of a culture that faded millennia ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T20:33:11-08:00","id":68782,"title":"","content":"A culture which, by the way, really didn't have any sense of racism-in fact, it's always surprising just how modern the idea of racism is(But let's avoid that). A certain form of nationalism, sure, but they didn't care about the peripheral details. They weren't really sexist, racist, or most of the other things. Either you contributed to the society in such a meaningful way you were recognized, or you didn't and you weren't. The entire Empire was surprisingly very meritocratic, granted with some of the guilds being more so than others, but it really came down to what you did for the standard of the scorpion.<br /> <br /> Mummies just don't care, and others who do have some big issues to deal with. A white plantation owner in early America is going to learn some damn respect for a mummy regardless of what shade of brown the mummy is or pay for his offenses against mummy and Judge brutally. A mummy does not give two shits about what happened to your damn precious towers and why that makes you reluctant to work with him because he looks like one of those damn Muslim folk-either you get in line or get out of the way, and he doesn't particularly care if you're the one who makes the choice. By the time they're weak enough for anyone to do anything, it's firmly entrenched in the minds of most that this is not a fellow you cross.<br /> <br /> Mummies are kind of badass that way. So when you play a mummy, don't play a black man, or an Iraqi, or anything like that. Play the concept-a brutal, pre-bronze age badass who's on a mission from things that make modern gods weep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T20:56:20-08:00","id":68788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions?p=68782#post68782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A culture which, by the way, really didn't have any sense of racism-in fact, it's always surprising just how modern the idea of racism is(But let's avoid that). A certain form of nationalism, sure, but they didn't care about the peripheral details. They weren't really sexist, racist, or most of the other things. Either you contributed to the society in such a meaningful way you were recognized, or you didn't and you weren't. The entire Empire was surprisingly very meritocratic, granted with some of the guilds being more so than others, but it really came down to what you did for the standard of the scorpion.<br /> <br /> Mummies just don't care, and others who do have some big issues to deal with. .</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that the empire basically considered anyone not of the Guilds to be a slave in the most traditional of sense and since Guilds haven't been recruiting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T20:57:26-08:00","id":68790,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not really a fan of the racial/cultural restrictions. Given the strong influence culture has on the development of personality and suchforth, it <i>seems</i> it would pretty seriously limit character concepts. Especially if you're not an expert on various African-area cultures, which I suspect most of us are not.<br /> <br /> Even if you can change the race in a physical sense, your character will still act/think/feel in a certain way, informed by what shreds of Memory they have managed to retain, which will only grow stronger as they regain Memory. Which makes it even more difficult.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm not saying Mummy is <i>bad</i> because of this. It makes sense within the game. It just seems it's going to be hard to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T22:42:43-08:00","id":68853,"title":"","content":"It's not a matter of it being African. We're talking about a culture that pre-dates cultures that the average person has very little knowledge about, and what experts in the field only see the edges of the elephant on. We have no idea just how the Sumerians, the Naquada, or any other culture truly lived like. We can recognize forms, but never really the life thereof. The Nameless Empire predates all of that, and on top of that is a fictional civilization.<br /> <br /> Mummy the Curse does a great job of detailing what that Iremite culture was like in terms of how its' people thought and responded to things, and Guildhalls only expanded that. You aren't playing an African, or even a normal pre-historic mortal, you are playing an Iremite, with the roadblocks for that culture laid out fairly clearly in the guilds, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> And if that's not enough, just establish that your character has been strongly influenced by the cultures you do know, grafting those customs and cultural attitudes onto what you've learned from Curse books. Hell, you don't even need to do that-just pick up and play, and develop a personality that you're comfortable with and leave it to the storyteller as you go along to find reasons you are the way you are, working with him as you feel necessary.<br /> <br /> Point is that these things aren't really issues, not in the conventional sense.<br /> <br /> @Shock: Yeah, for not being rulers, mummies still do have that sort of prejudice in mind. I can see the cults being given a certain leeway, but for the most part, the current world is always, in someways, a world of inferiors. Everything else that follows is just natural consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T05:35:21-08:00","id":68987,"title":"","content":"I can understand having Iram as a proto-culture for even South Africa, most of Europe, and some of Russia... But when we start hitting Latin America, China, and India is when my sense of disbelief starts to unravel. These are places with ancient cultures in their own rights. Assuming Iram spread this far kinda.. well... I just don't get it. <br /> <br /> And assuming that Mummies are people trying to take over the world? That's something I just have trouble wrapping my head around, given their small numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T09:58:02-08:00","id":69163,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I appreciate what they were TRYING to do with Mummy with regard to countering the immensely stupid racist garbage certain hate mongers try to say about Egypt (in brief, that the Egyptians were actually all white people because only white people could possibly have a powerful long lasting civilization that ancient- seriously fuck those people!). But I do not buy the argument that only Ancient Egypt has a &quot;gothic mystique&quot; and therefore the only possible kind of mummy that should be imagined is ancient Egyptian. The mummy archetype has certain themes inherent in the creature, yes, but those themes to do demand a strictly Egyptian asthetic. Given that the last game introduced mummies from across the Earth, having the new game localized in Egypt exclusively felt like a major step down to me. Which is why I see nothing wrong with assuming that at various points in its history the Nameless Empire covered much of the Earth. Nothing wrong with assuming the empire expanded and contracted just like the real world Egyptian Empire (during those occasions when Egypt decided to build an empire, of course), and with the monumental feats of magic available to the city it is not unreasonable to say that their borders to extend to impossible lengths and somewhat defy conventional wisdom (distance doesn't mean much if you can transport an army instantly through some mystic gateway). <br /> <br /> For me the situation decision was incredibly easy. I set my game in Las Vegas. When I came across this article: <a href=\"http://www.crystalinks.com/gc_egyptconnection.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.crystalinks.com/gc_egyptconnection.html</a><br /> <br /> I knew I had to make it a real thing in my games. And if that meant expanding the borders of Iram well beyond their established &quot;canonical&quot; area, then fuck the police, Iram was an empire upon which the barge of Ra never set! The advantages of being able to put a hidden beyond ancient tomb or temple literally wherever I wanted was obvious to me, and the &quot;problems&quot; of having a large and expansive Egyptian style Imperium were frankly nonexistent in my mind. Like our friends the Mage's Atlantis, Iram was swallowed up by black magic. Its fingerprint on the world could have been erased a long time ago. And having a greater diversity in the histories and origins of your players just seemed like common sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T10:07:37-08:00","id":69169,"title":"","content":"Irem itself didn't. However, people migrate, they travel, and they take important things with them, things such as the divinely powered corpses. Again, there's evidence that all of humanity really did begin in Africa and spread from there. The Nameless Empire story taps into that by positing that it consumed much of that seat, and that it's fall is a large motivator in the mass diaspora that lead to the filling up of the rest of the world, and assumes that the cults of naturally took their Arisen with them. Even beyond the idea of this original mass migration, mummies have always had their cults throughout the ages spread everywhere to claim their craft as appropriated by others. In the eight thousand years since the Nameless Empire, mummies have been moving around the globe answering the call of Sekhem and their Judges, which leads to movements most ordinary people wouldn't make.<br /> <br /> So, no, Irem had very clear, if large, boundaries that are clearly defined as being mostly African and Middle Eastern, but mummies didn't stay there after the Fall of the Empire. They went everywhere, and that's where people got the culture from.<br /> <br /> Also, mummies aren't trying to take over the world. While some guilds promote this more than others, the simple fact is is that the world already belongs to the Judges-that the rest of the world doesn't recognize that is of varying concern, but not to the point where they are 'taking it over' or even 'reclaiming' it(Well, okay, that's not entirely true, but it's true enough).<br /> <br /> Point is, it isn't really take over the world. There's no point to that. Take the best of the world and give it to the rightful owners? That's more like it. Give the occasional reminder of who it belogns to regardless of if they get it or not? Also more like it.<br /> <br /> Again, it's there in the book-mummies just don't have the same insecurities a lot of people do over these things. Their entirely different cultural background on top of the nature of their immortality just makes it so they don't give a shit about a lot of the superficial stuff we do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T15:36:45-08:00","id":69471,"title":"","content":"Well, ancient Egypt was, from my understanding, rather racially diverse. You had people of European origin, of south African origin, or the middle east. The problem, again, comes from Asia and the Americas.<br /> <br /> I mean, I kinda understand why they just wanted a single Iram and all. Its taking Atlantis from Mage, and putting it center stage. The hunt for artifacts and lost information of a bygone era is happening with a much sharper focus that I've found simply doesn't play out in Mage as well. Its the game of Occult Archaeology. Its just a very limited game, I think. It lacks the power and scope of Vampire, Mage, Changeling, Demon, Geist, Hunter, even Werewolf (I have trouble with werewolves in areas that, hey, no indigenous wolves). This is both a boon (tighter focus) and a bane (less replay value).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-10-2014, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T15:55:11-08:00","id":69476,"title":"","content":"It is a constant,but it need not always be a foreground aspect. Most of the stories I've worked out have had it as a backdrop to other stories.<br /> <br /> Still, we'll say fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T12:00:32-08:00","id":70754,"title":"","content":"I take from both approaches. My PC Meret is made up of soldiers and explorers who worked on the frontier of Irem, so I had to find a way to play it out. So, my Irem does have clear borders. One PC was involved with the Empire's attempts to conquer the Northmen, across the Caucasus and Black Sea. Though Irem had outposts there, the decentralized and nomadic nature of the proto-indo-europeans was impossible to conquer. The Empire met with the same resistance in modern Afghanistan and in the depths of Kush at the source of the nile, and the cradle of humanity itself. however, i also posited the idea that the Shan'Iatu had BOLD ambitions. For example, I have the idea for &quot;the furthest temple&quot;.. a place the shaniatu kept the most dangerous and valuable relics and mummies. too useful to be destroyed, but too unpredictable to be kept close, the Furthest Temple was constructed at the southern tip of south america, sometime just before the fall of irem (maybe 5000bc give or take, for the temple). similarly, provided they explain why their foreigner was valuable to a guild, Ive allowed white mummies and asian mummies.. but they're all Iremite. sure, there were cultures around near irem's end.. but.. none trafficed with the same darkness and blasphemous magics that Irem had. that is why those cultures survived, and Irem did not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}